# <PROJECT NAME> — project facts

Process rules live in the pipeline's shared rules file — OpenCode loads it from
`~/.config/opencode/AGENTS.md`, Claude Code from `~/.claude/rules/pipeline.md`;
both are the same file — and apply here unchanged. This file adds facts about
*this* project. It does not relax anything.

This file sits at the repo root on purpose: OpenCode and Claude Code both load
it from there (Claude Code through the `@AGENTS.md` import in `CLAUDE.md`).
Keep it the single source of project facts for both tools.

## Pipeline layout

| Path | What | Used by |
|---|---|---|
| `.handoff/` | plans, specs, reports — the shared record | both tools |
| `.workitems/` | ingested tickets; `TRACKING.md` says whether any exist | both tools |
| `.opencode/` | OpenCode project overrides (models, permissions) | OpenCode |
| `.claude/` | Claude Code project settings | Claude Code |
| `AGENTS.md` / `CLAUDE.md` | project facts / Claude's import of them | both tools |

