## T3 floor — ALWAYS CRITICAL

**This section is a human decision. Do not let an agent fill it in.**

Any slice touching a path or concern below is tier **T3** regardless of how
small the change looks. The architect may escalate above this list. The
architect may not go below it, and may not split a slice so that part of it
escapes the list.

**Paths:**

- `<path/to/critical/module>` — <why>

**Concerns, wherever they appear:**

- <e.g. anything that writes to persistent storage irreversibly>
- <e.g. authentication, key material, signature verification>
- <e.g. any code path reached during recovery from a failure>

**Why each of these is here:** <one line each. A floor whose reasoning is
undocumented gets quietly eroded the first time it is inconvenient.>

